# Build output.
#
# dist/ is generated entirely by build/build.py from src/ and build/template.html,
# so it is reproducible and does not belong in the repo. Run the build to produce it:
#
#   cd build && python build.py
#
# Untracked 2026-09-25. Note that the previously committed bundles and zips remain
# in earlier commits -- ignoring the folder stops future churn, it does not rewrite
# history.
dist/

# IDE settings. JetBrains project files are per-developer; the module paths and
# workspace.xml in particular differ on every machine.
.idea/

# Claude Code machine-local settings. Deliberately narrower than ignoring all of
# .claude/ -- a shared project-level .claude/settings.json can still be committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
